@startuml EventPulse_Login_To_Fulfilment_Monolith

title EventPulse — Login to Order Fulfilment (Happy Path)

actor User
participant "Frontend" as UI
participant "API\n(Controllers)" as API
participant "Services" as SVC
database "MariaDB" as DB

== Login ==
User -> UI : Email + password
UI -> API : POST /api/auth/login
API -> SVC : AuthService.login()
SVC -> DB : Find user by email
DB --> SVC : User
SVC -> SVC : Check password + issue JWT
SVC --> API : token
API --> UI : 200 OK { token }
UI --> User : Dashboard

== Browse events ==
User -> UI : Browse / select tickets
UI -> API : GET /api/events
API -> SVC : EventService.getEvents()
SVC -> DB : Load events
DB --> SVC : Events
SVC --> API : Event list
API --> UI : Events
UI --> User : Show events + availability

== Book ==
User -> UI : Confirm booking
UI -> API : POST /api/bookings
API -> SVC : BookingService.createBooking()
SVC -> DB : Reserve seats, save booking (PENDING)
DB --> SVC : Booking saved
SVC --> API : Booking (pending payment)
API --> UI : Booking created
UI --> User : Go to payment

== Pay ==
User -> UI : Pay
UI -> API : POST /api/payments
API -> SVC : PaymentService.processPayment()
SVC -> SVC : Charge payment provider
SVC -> DB : Save transaction (SUCCESS)\nConfirm booking (CONFIRMED)
DB --> SVC : Updated
SVC --> API : Payment + booking confirmed
API --> UI : Order confirmed

== Fulfil ==
SVC -> SVC : NotificationService\n(generate ticket)
SVC -> User : Email / SMS ticket
UI --> User : Confirmation + ticket

note right of API
  Login is implemented.
  Events → book → pay → fulfil are planned.
end note

@enduml
